  "_svg_note": "The published .drawio.svg is exported by hand from the .drawio in draw.io (File > Export as > SVG). Re-export it whenever this spec changes.",
  "_intent": "How the components fit together, not how they are configured. Sizes, counts, engine versions, encryption and retention live in the written design (Solution Design section 4), not here.",
  "_layout_notes": [
    "Subnet containers carry a pale tier tint; resources carry the strong colour. Nesting shows the tier, so the fills only need to separate resource from subnet.",
    "The IGW straddles the VPC boundary because that is what it attaches to.",
    "The ALB and the DB subnet group straddle their two subnets, placed below the label band so they do not clip it. That straddle is the point of the diagram for AT3 tasks 7 and 9.",
    "Outbound routing and LDAP leave the private-app-a SUBNET, not the instance \u2014 it is the subnet's route table that sends them. This also keeps three edges off the EC2 box.",
    "Straight lines beat routed ones. Align the centres of any two boxes an edge joins, so the renderer draws one segment rather than a dog-leg \u2014 a diagram reads far faster when the connectors are straight. Keep the whole thing tight enough to sit on one page."
  ],
